# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitattributes -- line endings for the files whose bytes matter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Template from unicef-drp/cso-toolkit: templates/gitattributes/project.gitattributes
#
# A Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default)
# checks text files out with CRLF. For most files that is harmless; for
# these it is not, so they stay LF on every platform:
#   - the pre-push hook: sh on macOS and Linux cannot run a script whose
#     lines end in \r;
#   - the vendored cso-toolkit helpers: their bytes must stay those of the
#     release named in 00_functions/.toolkit_manifest.yml;
#   - provenance sidecars: they are read and compared as committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.githooks/**        text eol=lf
*.sh                text eol=lf
00_functions/**     text eol=lf
*.provenance.json   text eol=lf
